  "difficulty": "Medium",
  "topic": "stack",
  "statement": "You are given an array of strings tokens that represents an arithmetic expression in a Reverse Polish Notation. Evaluate the expression. Return an integer that represents the value of the expression. Valid operators are +, -, *, and /. Each operand may be an integer or another expression. Division between two integers should truncate toward zero.",
  "function_name": "eval_rpn",
